---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="ChartsAI Source Code & Sample Data — Free to Reuse"
  description="Download the MIT-licensed source for ChartsAI’s eight chart makers and printable habit tracker. Inspect the calculations and reuse original sample datasets."
  ><article class="container prose-page">
    <span class="eyebrow">OPEN TO LEARN FROM</span><h1>
      Look under<br /><em>the picture.</em>
    </h1><p class="intro-text">
      The tools are free to use. The implementation is open to inspect, adapt and build on.
    </p><p class="byline">Version 0.5.1 · SupaMakers · September 8, 2026</p><a
      class="button"
      href="/downloads/chartsai-source.zip"
      download>Download the source ZIP ↓</a
    ><h2>What is included?</h2><ul>
      <li>
        Eight chart editors, including histogram, box plot, scatter, bar and Pareto, Apache ECharts configuration, three visual themes
        and export logic.
      </li><li>The spreadsheet import preview, number parsing and data validation.</li><li>
        The printable habit tracker with calendar logic and PDF generation.
      </li><li>Static pages, original sample data, methodology notes and meaningful calculation tests.</li>
    </ul><h2>Run it locally</h2><pre><code>npm install
npm run prepare:assets
npm run dev</code></pre><p>
      The project uses Astro, React, TypeScript and Apache ECharts. The README contains build instructions,
      input limits and deployment notes. Node.js 22.12 or newer is required by the current build tooling.
    </p><h2>Built on Apache ECharts</h2><p>
      ChartsAI uses ECharts’ built-in scatter, radar, line, bar and boxplot series for geometry, axes, tooltips and
      rendering. Examples are rendered as SVG during the site build; interactive charts and all user data stay
      in the browser. You can download a chart’s ECharts option JSON from its editor.
    </p><p>
      <a href="https://echarts.apache.org/">Apache ECharts</a> is licensed under Apache 2.0. Third-party notices
      are included in the source archive.
    </p><h2>License and attribution</h2><p>
      The original ChartsAI code and fictional sample data are released under the MIT license. Keep the
      license notice when redistributing substantial portions of the code. Third-party libraries and fonts
      have their own licenses. Charts generated from your own data do not require a ChartsAI credit. Public datasets retain their own attribution requirements.
    </p><p>
      If the tools help your work, a link to <a href="https://www.chartsai.com/">ChartsAI</a> or a mention of <a
        href="https://www.supamakers.com/">SupaMakers</a
      > is appreciated. It is optional for your exported charts and printables.
    </p><p>
      <a href="https://github.com/supamakers/chartsai-studio">Browse the code and contribute on GitHub ↗</a>
    </p><h2>50 worked chart examples</h2><p>
      The <a href="/examples/">example library</a> includes original fictional datasets, worked calculations, reusable
      chart exports and exact editor starting points. Generated showcase assets are recreated by the asset preparation
      command.
    </p><h2>Attributed public datasets</h2><p>The <a href="/datasets/">public-data collection</a> contains Iris, Wine, Glass Identification, Seeds and Abalone from UCI. These datasets are CC BY 4.0, separately from our MIT code and fictional examples. Keep the original authors, source and license attribution and identify your changes. Each resource documents the pinned source file and chart selection.</p><h2>Small fictional datasets to try</h2><ul>
      <li>
        <a href="/samples/dot-scores.csv" download>Class scores — dot-plot CSV</a>
      </li><li>
        <a href="/samples/dot-delivery.csv" download>Delivery times — dot-plot CSV</a>
      </li><li>
        <a href="/samples/radar-skills.csv" download>Team skills — radar-chart CSV</a>
      </li><li>
        <a href="/samples/radar-products.csv" download>Product ratings — radar-chart CSV</a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="/samples/line-monthly.csv" download>Monthly orders — line-graph CSV</a>
      </li>
    </ul><p>
      All these datasets are fictional. They illustrate tool behavior and should not be presented as research
      findings.
    </p><h2>Found something to improve?</h2><p>
      We welcome reproducible feedback about data handling, calculations and accessibility. <a
        href="mailto:support@chartsai.com">Send us a small example</a
      >, preferably with fictional values.
    </p>
  </article></Layout
>
